+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  The optional ``canonical`` option describes the
+   type represented by the alias and is displayed in the signature after the
+   alias name.  It is parsed as a type annotation, so referenced types can be
+   cross-referenced normally.  A description body may also be supplied.
+
+   For example::
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+         Identifier for a user.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias.  This option is optional.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the alias is defined.  The default value is
